.TH "GLESHA-VERSION" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glesha-version \- show the executable version and build revision
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glesha version [GLOBAL OPTIONS]
.br
.B glesha \-v
.br
.B glesha \-version
.br
.B glesha \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
All forms print glesha VERSION (GIT_SHA) and exit successfully.
Development builds print glesha dev (unknown) unless values were embedded
at build time. This command does not load configuration or credentials and
makes no cloud requests. Extra positional arguments are rejected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config FILE
Accepted without loading the file.
.TP
.B \-\-env FILE
Accepted without reading credentials.
.TP
.B \-L, \-\-log\-level LEVEL
Accepted; no operation diagnostics are produced.
.TP
.B \-\-color MODE
Accepted; version output is plain ASCII.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command help and examples.
.TP
.B \-v, \-version, \-\-version
Print the executable version and build revision.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha version

glesha \-v

glesha \-version

glesha \-\-version

glesha help version
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. 2 for invalid usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha-help (1)
